{title: My Father My Friend}
{artist: Dustin Kleinschmidt}
{genre: Modern Worship}
{style: Ballad}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}
{license: WorshipCommons License 1.0}
{copyright: © 1995 Dustin Kleinschmidt}
{c: © 1995 Dustin Kleinschmidt · WorshipCommons License 1.0 (free for worship) https://worshipcommons.org/license · Source: https://worshipcommons.org/songs/my-father-my-friend--fU10ve-8Xm/}
{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]In the still of the night, [F/A]I know you're holding me tight.
[Bb]So I can rest in your arms, [C]for you protect me from harm.
[F]Your love has carried me through [F/A]when pain was all that I knew.
[Bb]I do rejoice in your grace, [C]for we will see face to face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]And I will [Bb]sing this song of [Dm]love
To my Savior on [Bb]high, I could not praise you e[F]nough
[F]And I will [Bb]lift my voice a[Dm]gain
You’ve given yourself for [Bb]me, You are my Father, [C]my [F]friend
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]In the warmth of the day, [F/A]I see you leading my way;
[Bb]So I will trust you to guide, [C]as I learn each day to a[F]bide.
[F]You go before every step, [F/A]and in your presence I'm kept.
[Bb]Wherever you choose to lead, [C]You are everything I [F]need.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[F]When I’m weak, you are [Bb]strong,
You’ve been faithful all a[Dm]long
I will trust, I will not fear,
[Bb]For you are close, for you are [F]here
[F]When I’m weak, you are [Bb]strong,
You’ve been faithful all a[Dm]long
I will trust, I will not fear,
[Bb]For you are close, for you are [F]here
{end_of_bridge}
